D</article-title><source>Neurology</source><year>2006</year><volume>67</volume><fpage>528</fpage><lpage>530</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16894124</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1212/01.wnl.0000228218.68451.31</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bartha</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Rupsingh</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Rylett</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Wells</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Borrie</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>High field (1)H MRS of the hippocampus after donepezil treatment in Alzheimer disease</article-title><source>Prog Neuropsychopharmacol Biol Psychiatry</source><year>2008</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>786</fpage><lpage>793</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18252268</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.pnpbp.2007.12.011</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Codita</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Winblad</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Mohammed</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Of mice and men: more neurobiology in dementia</article-title><source>Curr Opin Psychiatry</source><year>2006</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>555</fpage><lpage>563</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17012931</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/01.yco.0000245757.06374.6a</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Games</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Buttini</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kobayashi</surname><given-n